Description: Fix t_proxy helper for Python 3.12 and later
 ssl.wrap_socket() was deprecated since Python 3.7 and removed in Python
 3.12.  t_proxy.py starts util/wsgiref-kdcproxy.py, which still calls it,
 so the test dies with:
 .
   AttributeError: module 'ssl' has no attribute 'wrap_socket'
 .
 Replace the call with an ssl.SSLContext, which is available since Python
 3.2 and works on every supported interpreter.
Author: deepin-ci-robot <packages@deepin.org>
Last-Update: 2026-11-24
---
diff --git a/src/util/wsgiref-kdcproxy.py b/src/util/wsgiref-kdcproxy.py
index 5875969..c19119c 100755
--- a/src/util/wsgiref-kdcproxy.py
+++ b/src/util/wsgiref-kdcproxy.py
@@ -14,6 +14,8 @@ else:
     pem = '*'
 
 server = make_server('localhost', port, kdcproxy.Application())
-server.socket = ssl.wrap_socket(server.socket, certfile=pem, server_side=True)
+context = ssl.SSLContext(ssl.PROTOCOL_TLS_SERVER)
+context.load_cert_chain(certfile=pem)
+server.socket = context.wrap_socket(server.socket, server_side=True)
 os.write(sys.stdout.fileno(), b'proxy server ready\n')
 server.serve_forever()
